---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Every statement here is something the product does today; the DECISIONS.md
// entry behind each is noted beside it so a change there can be found here.
const sections = [
  {
    id: "access",
    title: "Access is read-only, and granted by you",
    points: [
      // §147, the consent callback binds the tenant
      "An admin in your tenant consents to Cleave's Entra application. The tenant is taken from that consent, never typed in, so a connection cannot point at someone else's directory.",
      "Cleave reads through a custom role that lists read actions only. It cannot change a setting, start a resource or move data.",
      // §147
      "A consent link carries a one-time value, spent before any call to Microsoft, so a link cannot be replayed.",
      "Nothing is installed in your cloud. There are no agents.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "data",
    title: "What is stored, and what is never asked for",
    points: [
      "Each scan stores what Azure returned, verbatim, so a new rule can judge an old capture without reading your cloud again.",
      // §176, backlog Tier 3
      "Key Vault keys and secrets are read as management metadata only. Their values are never requested, and neither is the action that returns application settings and connection strings.",
      "A setting Cleave could not read is recorded as unread, with the reason. It is never stored as a pass.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "isolation",
    title: "Each organization's data is isolated twice",
    points: [
      "The API derives your organization from your verified sign-in on every request.",
      "The database enforces the same boundary with row-level security, under a role that cannot read another organization's rows even if a query asked for them.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "accounts",
    title: "Accounts and people",
    points: [
      // §214, §217
      "Sign in with Microsoft, Google or a password. Two-factor authentication is enforced by the API, not only by the sign-in screen.",
      // §162
      "Colleagues join by invitation. The invitation token is single-use and stored only as a hash.",
      // §163
      "Every change a person makes is written to an append-only audit log that owners and admins can read.",
      // §211
      "An auditor reads a sealed package through a grant bound to their verified email. It expires, it can be revoked, and each read is logged.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "outbound",
    title: "What leaves Cleave",
    points: [
      // §164
      "Webhooks go only to public HTTPS addresses. Each delivery is signed, pinned to the address that was checked, and never follows a redirect.",
      "The site you are reading sets no cookies and runs no analytics.",
    ],
  },
];

const processors = [
  ["Vercel", "Hosts the web application"],
  ["Railway", "Runs the API and scan workers"],
  ["Supabase", "PostgreSQL database and authentication"],
  ["Microsoft, Google", "Sign-in, when you choose them"],
];
---

<Base
  title="Security · Cleave"
  description="How Cleave reaches your Azure estate, what it stores, what it never asks for, and how each organization's data is isolated."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6 lg:pt-20">
    <h1
      class="rise max-w-3xl text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.05] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-balance sm:text-6xl"
    >
      How Cleave touches your cloud.
    </h1>
    <p class="rise mt-6 max-w-[56ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted" style="--i:1">
      A security product asks for access to everything you run. Here is exactly what it does with
      it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div
    class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,3fr)_minmax(0,9fr)] lg:py-24"
  >
    <nav aria-label="On this page" class="hidden lg:block">
      <ul class="sticky top-28 space-y-2.5 border-l border-line text-[15px]">
        {
          sections.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${s.id}`} class="-ml-px block border-l border-transparent pl-4 text-muted hover:border-fg hover:text-fg">
                {s.title.split(",")[0]}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
        <li>
          <a href="#processors" class="-ml-px block border-l border-transparent pl-4 text-muted hover:border-fg hover:text-fg">
            Who processes data
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      {
        sections.map((s) => (
          <section id={s.id} aria-labelledby={`${s.id}-t`} class="reveal">
            <h2 id={`${s.id}-t`} class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em] text-balance">
              {s.title}
            </h2>
            <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4">
              {s.points.map((p) => (
                <li class="relative max-w-[68ch] pl-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
                  <span class="absolute top-[0.7em] left-0 h-px w-2.5 bg-brand" aria-hidden="true" />
                  {p}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </section>
        ))
      }

      <section id="processors" aria-labelledby="processors-t" class="reveal">
        <h2 id="processors-t" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em]">
          Who processes data for Cleave
        </h2>
        <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-[14px] border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2">
          {
            processors.map(([name, role]) => (
              <div class="bg-surface p-5">
                <dt class="font-medium">{name}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-[15px] text-muted">{role}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
